msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:226
#. Diagram label
msgid "Certified and signed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Certifier"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:165
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computed from six facts read off the records — report status, data hash known, unexecuted cases, the checker's agreement, failed and passed cases — by the table the plan's `exitCriteria` names (resolved dynamically; if unresolvable, routes to undetermined and never silently falls back to default). Supplying the branch by hand is refused."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:133
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every case in dependency order. A case is executed or explicitly `skipped` with its reason; a case that simply has no verdict is a finding, because it cannot be told from a case nobody ran."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:132
#. Diagram label
msgid "Execute every case, or skip it with a reason"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Executing a `test-plan/v1` against a system under test and taking the result to a certification decision: requested by (or for) the system, run by a tester, re-executed in sample by an untainted checker, decided by a certifier through the plan's exit-criteria table, and signed through `qa-report-signing.bpmn`. You are in this process when somebody wants a system — a skill, an agent, a tool, a machine, an IG or a process — certified against a named plan. Executing a plan with no certification in view is still this process; it ends at `undetermined` or `refused` without anything being signed. The run, the report and the certification are three records, and they point backwards: the run at the plan, the report at the run, the certification at the report. The certification is a judgement and lives under the declared `attestations` graph, on main; the report is derived and lives on the `qa-reports` branch."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:164
#. Diagram label
msgid "Exit criteria met?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:216
#. Diagram label
msgid "File the signed certification [qa-attestations/v1]"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:154
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Given the plan, the bound data and a sample of case ids — not the report. Says `agree`, `disagree` or `unknown`; `unknown` (could not run) is said as plainly as a disagreement, because the table reads both the same way and an unknown read as agreement certifies on one party's word."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Name the plan by id AND version, and the system under test by actor id. The actor must carry the `systemUnderTest` facet: an actor that has not said it can be tested is not run against a plan by default. The bean this instance tracks is claimed here."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:123
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per bean `vm6m`: a fixed set is a committed path and counts as evidence only once reviewed; a generated set is template + params + seed and is never materialised. Both feed the run's data hash, and nothing that feeds the process hash may feed it too."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:153
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-execute a sample, blind to the tester's verdicts"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:175
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the certification decision [attestations]"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:186
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the refusal, with the failing cases"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:196
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record why it could not be decided"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:229
#. Diagram label
msgid "Refused"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:244
#. Diagram label
msgid "refused"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:102
#. Diagram label
msgid "Request certification of the system against plan P"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:65
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requester / system under test"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "Resolve the plan [test-plan/v1]"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the plan against the system: resolves it, binds its fixed or generated test data, executes every case or skips it with a reason, and writes the `folio-test-run/v1` and the `test-report/v1`. Untainted from the system under test — never the same actor — and it does not certify: what it writes is what the certifier decides on."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:206
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sign the certification"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Signs the certification and files it. Reached only from `certified`: a refusal and an undetermined result are recorded by the certifier and signed by nobody. The signature itself is `qa-report-signing.bpmn`, called unchanged, whose own gateway chooses the API or a human release authority by the signer's reach."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Test-plan execution"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Test-plan execution — request, run, check, certify, sign"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Tester"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The accountable party for the decision, a specialisation of the stakeholder. The gateway is computed from the plan's exit-criteria table; what the certifier adds, and what makes it a judgement, is recording the decision under their name. Never the tester and never the system under test."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:176
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The judgement: the certifier records, under their own name, that the system meets plan P at this version on this run. It is written under the declared `attestations` graph beside the other judgements, never on the `qa-reports` branch with derived results. A user task, so no agent or pipeline can fill it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan parses, names at least one `req:` requirement, its `exitCriteria` resolves to a decision in a `.dmn` that exists, and its `scope.kind` is the system's facet kind. A plan that does not resolve is not run — `test-plan-resolves` audits the same join afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:144
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The run records `plan {id, version}` and `sut {actor, version, reach}` with its data and process hashes; the report rolls up per plan, never across plans, and goes to the `qa-reports` branch at `tests/plan/sut/run/`. No verdict in it may name the system under test as its reviewer."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:217
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signed certification goes under the declared `attestations` graph on main (owner ruling D2 (a), D5 default), pointing at the report it certifies. The bean resolves here, once the process has actually finished."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The system under test, or whoever speaks for it, asking for certification against plan P at a named version. Its only task is the request, and that is the design rather than an omission: the system under test never writes a verdict about itself, so after this lane it is the SUBJECT of the process and never a performer in it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/test-plan-execution.bpmn:197
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The third state: which fact kept the table from deciding — a run not finished, an unknown data hash, an unexecuted case, a checker that disagreed or could not run, or nothing passed. A note and not a resolution, because the request is still open: it needs a re-run or an adjudication, not a verdict."
msgstr ""

